` EVERY QUEST IS PICKED UP. the quest of a round shows up as a pickup beside the board, and nothing
` else: no name, no badge, and nothing on the board. it only starts when the cursor steps out onto
` the pickup, and stepping out onto it again puts it down. a quest that fails starts over without
` having to be picked up again, and QUEST_REARM is how questInitNow knows to do that. a quest that
` was put down, or that a game was loaded with, waits to be picked up. one that the debug window
` starts is picked up already.
global QUEST_REARM = 0

global QUEST_INIT_DUE = 0 `1 when the quest has to be set up, the next time that the board is settled
global QUEST_HOLD = 0 `1 while the board is growing, when nothing can be set up on it
global QUEST_SWEEP_DUE = 0 `1 when the fish that only a quest puts on the board have to be taken off of it, the next time that it is settled

` THE UPGRADE SCREEN WAITS FOR THE SWEEP. when a quest that was finished is done with, at the end
` of its round, the fish that only a quest puts on the board have to be off of it before the
` upgrade screen comes up, and that has to wait for the board to settle. questHoldsRound, in
` fish_routines_quests, is what frame_score asks. a quest that is not finished carries on into the
` next round, so there is nothing to wait for then.
global QUEST_LEAVE_UNTIL = 0 `the upgrade screen does not come up before this, in milliseconds of the game
global QUEST_LEAVE_TIME = 550 `how long the bubbles get to be seen

global QUEST_PICK_CELL = -1 `the cell that the pickup is beside. it is the last cell of a row.
global QUEST_REWARD = 0 `what the quest that was just finished paid out
global QUEST_FLOOR_PERCENT = 5 `a quest never pays less than this much of what the whole round takes

