` HOW A QUEST IS DRAWN. there are three piles of things to draw with, and a quest takes from them
` on every frame: squares of light under the fish, pictures on top of the fish, and numbers on top
` of those. whatever a frame does not take is hidden. so a quest never has to keep track of what it
` has on the screen, and nothing is left behind when it ends. questGlowCell, questIconAt and
` questNumberAt, in fish_routines_quests, hand them out.
global QUEST_GLOW_MAX = 120
global dim QUEST_GLOW_SPRITES(120)
global QUEST_GLOW_N = 0
global QUEST_GLOW_SHOWN = 0 `how many the last frame took
global QUEST_ICON_MAX = 48
global dim QUEST_ICON_SPRITES(48)
global QUEST_ICON_N = 0
global QUEST_ICON_SHOWN = 0
global QUEST_NUM_MAX = 8
global dim QUEST_NUM_TEXTS(8)
global QUEST_NUM_N = 0
global QUEST_NUM_SHOWN = 0

` THE ZONES. the squares of light are drawn by an effect of their own, QuestZoneEffect.fx: a faint
` wash of color, with an outline around it that the water pushes about. the outline of the zone
` that the cursor is on is drawn stronger, and the wash inside stays as it is.
` questZone, in fish_routines_quests, tells the effect how to draw each one.

` STAYING OUT OF THE WAY. a quest only draws what it cannot be played without: the thing itself, and
` a ring around a fish that it has marked. everything that only explains it, like where its thing
` is headed, or where its thing must not go, is drawn while the cursor is on the thing, and at no
` other time. QUEST_FOCUS is 1 on a frame when the cursor is on a fish that the quest marked, or on
` a fish of one of the quest's own kinds. a quest that has some other thing to point at, like the
` shark, works that out for itself when it draws.
global QUEST_FOCUS = 0

` A LOOK AT THE QUEST. while the cursor is out on the pickup of a quest that has not been started,
` the name of the quest shows up where its badge will go, with a question mark after it, in a puff
` of bubbles. when the cursor comes away again, it fizzles out. starting the quest gives the name
` a punch, and a lot more bubbles, and it stays. QUEST_PREVIEW is 1 on a frame that the name is
` showing this way.
global QUEST_PREVIEW = 0

` POINTING THE QUEST OUT. while the cursor is out on the pickup of a quest that is running,
` everything that the quest has on the board is pointed out: QUEST_HILITE is 1, which lights up
` every fish of the quest's own kinds, makes the outlines of the fish that it marked strong, and
` counts as the cursor being on the thing, so that whatever explains the quest is drawn too.
global QUEST_HILITE = 0

` SLIDING AND GLIDING. a thing of a quest that moves by itself does not jump from cell to cell.
` a fish of the quest's that trades places with the fish next to it, like the turtle, slides: the
` two pictures start where the other one was, and ease to where they belong. questSlideStart
` starts it, and questStepSlide plays it. a picture that is not a fish, like the shark, glides:
` where it is drawn chases the cell that it is on. QUEST_GLIDE_X# and QUEST_GLIDE_Y# are where it
` is drawn.
global QUEST_SLIDE_MS = -1 `when the slide started, or -1 when there is none
global QUEST_SLIDE_TIME = 260 `how long it takes, in milliseconds
global QUEST_SLIDE_A = 0 `the two cells
global QUEST_SLIDE_B = 0
global QUEST_GLIDE_X# = 0
global QUEST_GLIDE_Y# = 0

global QUEST_ZONE_FX_ID
